  "description": "Accelerated Weathering of Limestone (AWL) process: captures CO2 from coastal biomass plants, converts to bicarbonate via limestone + seawater, stores permanently in ocean as stable calcium bicarbonate. Delivers durable ocean CDR (>10k years) with marine life co-benefits and acidification mitigation. Scalable modular design, low energy, minimal infrastructure. Strong focus on measurable MRV (pH, alkalinity, carbon flux).",
